SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Implemented the Ingest-X-Ray page as an adaptive SwiftUI surface (macOS regular /
iPad regular / iPhone compact, ADR-002/006), driven by an @Observable model over two
KMP-style data-source seams (ADR-004 — zero networking in the view). It reproduces the
full web page: the title/subtitle chrome (web PageContainer), the controls bar
(GlassPanel1 — vehicle picker + window + bucket selectors, web XRayControls), the
"select a vehicle" prompt (GlassPanel2, shown until a vehicle is chosen), and — once a
vehicle is selected — the header stat strip (web XRayHeader: total-samples /
distinct-fields / window tiles), the bucketed sample-count bar chart (GlassPanel3, web
XRayBucketChart, rendered with the P3 native Swift Charts wrapper TSBarChart — never a
WKWebView), and the sortable per-field statistics table (GlassPanel4, web
XRayFieldsTable, the P3 adaptive TSDataTable). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names. SI N/A — ingest X-Ray is sample-count
telemetry metadata (counts + timestamps + a value_kind enum, no physical units); the
display-boundary formatters render grouped integers, relative/absolute times, and the
value_kind label.

The web `useIngestXRay` query is re-keyed in SwiftUI: the model exposes a `reloadToken`
(vehicle|window|bucket) and the view drives `.task(id: reloadToken) { reloadXRay() }`,
the native analogue of TanStack Query re-keying. The bucket selector only offers buckets
`< window` (web disables `BUCKET_SECS >= WINDOW_SECS`) and a window change clamps the
selection so the live combination is always server-valid.

OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`.
That path is NOT a project.yml source group — the only compiled `TeslaSync/*` groups are
widget-primitives / dashboard-widgets / feature-views / misc-surfaces / shared-surfaces.
The repo's real, compiled canonical admin-page home — proven by the sibling DONE pages
(DLQInspector, LiveSignalInspector, FeatureFlags, …) — is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/
Admin/` (`Sources` is a recursive project.yml source path). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — the faithful equivalent of `Features/Admin`.
Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an
allowed file). This mapping is the only deviation from the literal prompt path.

